hip.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fe6fafebab89059cb03481d9b072ac3bd7be3a526191b23ac64571c810ca9976","event_uuid":"32fa1fb0-8621-4511-9ac1-0d8883d33158","position":{"commit_sha":"6ac86b8cea27b099caa544b3d663f191e88a6cf5","position":"1786069910406116001-32fa1fb0-8621-4511-9ac1-0d8883d33158"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5f2f2104fc3a0a5e89164e1679aa39c1c1cb2d67d2f4e795434bf40fbf79a04a","event_uuid":"3f6e8960-629a-4007-ab66-8d90556cf347","position":{"commit_sha":"7cbf570290c68ab060f97eb2d80c83fa86afcbc2","position":"1786070004917232001-3f6e8960-629a-4007-ab66-8d90556cf347"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3cbda6c4ecfad2d47eb8b324b70e456aa9719122433d0992db0c089664e5d865","event_uuid":"9c3f667d-45a3-4695-aa25-f8870f60a622","position":{"commit_sha":"262b5093bb9cf9d34f8105faf70fafe440675b08","position":"1786072788731163001-9c3f667d-45a3-4695-aa25-f8870f60a622"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## MEASURED EVIDENCE CONTRADICTS THIS TICKET'S PREMISE — and it came from this ticket's own instrument\n\nThis ticket asserts, in its title, that the completion verifier \"exhausts its turn budget on\ngenuine breadth, NOT on a loop\".\n\nNew measurement, 2026-08-05, from the completion-verification run on ticket\n94a3-1323-3497-4f59:\n\n    max_consecutive_repeat = 131\n    on ONE identical `search_files` signature, out of 260 total tool calls\n    failed at the DEFAULT step budget, then failed IDENTICALLY at REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS=1200\n\n131 consecutive repeats of the same call signature is a non-progressing loop by any reasonable\ndefinition. Raising the budget \ndid not change the outcome, which is the discriminating test between\n\"needs more room\" and \"is not progressing\" — breadth would have completed with 1200 steps.\n\n## The irony worth recording\n\nThe telemetry that produced this number is THIS TICKET'S OWN WORK. a89d's single landed change\n(commit 5f00bf5253, \"report tool-call repetition on exhaustion\") satisfied AC5 by adding exactly\nthis repetition reporting. The instrument built to characterise the failure has now measured a\nfailure mode the ticket's title rules out.\n\nThat is a good outcome for the instrument and a problem for the premise.\n\n## What this means — two readings, not yet distinguished\n\n1. **The premise is simply wrong** and the exhaustion always was (or has become) a loop. If so\n   this ticket's ACs 1-4 are aimed at the wrong target: \"make evidence-gathering directed\" and\n   \"stop treating output_token_limit as a hard ceiling\" do not fix a 131x repeat.\n2. **There are TWO failure modes** that both surface as budget exhaustion — genuine breadth (the\n   9fd4 / db1c cases this ticket cites) and a non-progressing loop (the 94a3 case). If so, both\n   are real and this ticket should be scoped to the first, with the loop tracked separately.\n\nI did NOT determine which. Reading 2 is plausible because the cited cases predate today's\nmeasurement, and nobody has re-run 9fd4 or db1c with the repetition telemetry in place — which\nis now the obvious next step and is cheap.\n\n## Related\n\nBug 46a2-9c1a-d855-4706 was filed today for the loop, from the 94a3 run, with a loop-guard design.\nIf reading 1 holds, 46a2 and this ticket are the same bug and one should be closed as duplicate.\nIf reading 2 holds, they are siblings. Deciding that is the first thing to do here.\n\nUNVERIFIED LEAD, flagged rather than asserted: the looping call is `search_files`, and commit\n85805e02f1 (\"bf31: search_files must not fake '(no matches)'\") changed that tool's behaviour\ntoday. Whether a more honest empty result changes retry behaviour is speculation — I have not\ntested it, and it should be checked before being believed.","timestamp":1785954502545754001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Settling the question raised by 46a2-9c1a-d855-4706 (does the 131x-repeat measurement contradict this ticket's breadth premise?): BOTH exhaustion modes are real — they are siblings, not one bug. Instrumented evidence from the c827 investigation: of four traced exhaustions of this gate, three LOOPED (one repeated an identical search_files call 144x; 46a2's case repeated one 131x; bf31's was a 4-call cycle repeated 31-37x) and ONE was genuine breadth (258 calls, 238 distinct, ratio 0.922, minimum 24-window distinct-ratio 0.833 — no loop by any metric). This ticket's premise holds for that run class; re-scope it to the breadth mode. The loop mode is being fixed by epic 9b71-55b3-1bd1-4a97 (windowed distinct-ratio detector + route-to-recovery actuator). Per the operator's stated intent, a breadth exhaustion under a budget that bounds FAILURES is correct behaviour — this ticket's remaining scope is making evidence-gathering more directed, not raising ceilings.","timestamp":1785954775605464001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA — completion-validator incident reclassified; no recovery-code fix is yet justified.\n\nObserved ordering: the second 8322 completion verdict was emitted at event timestamp 1786063291486790001. It rejected Gerrit change 1455 / both +1 votes / run 31131797081 / mirror SHA 81b3b59294 as ticket-only evidence. The exact `[operator-attested]` tag was added afterward at 1786063328784010001 (37.30s later). ADR 0043 and `completion_verifier.md:81-86` deliberately classify every untagged criterion as codebase-verifiable, for which a ticket comment alone is insufficient. Therefore that recorded rejection was intended strict-tag behavior, not proof of a bounded-recovery defect.\n\nDiscriminating runtime probes used the production completion model `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` with temperature 0 and the current tagged 8322 material. Current gatherer -> current finalizer passed the concrete operator attestation 3/3, emitted `kind=operator-attested, met=true`, and cited the ticket provenance. The same pipeline with an experimental co-located gatherer rule also passed 3/3. A direct current-finalizer probe given the exact tagged criterion and concrete bounded evidence likewise passed 3/3. Thus provenance is neither omitted nor truncated in the current tagged path, and the finalizer does not reject it. These outcomes reject the planned recovery/finalizer RCA.\n\nThe genuine defect exposed by the incident is the remediation-contract mismatch at `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:48-65`: every FAIL says concrete ticket-comment evidence will be considered on retry, but it omits the exact `[operator-attested]` tag prerequisite for external evidence. The operator followed that guidance, added a concrete comment, and received the contractually correct second FAIL because the criterion was still untagged. This is multi-file contract drift relative to ADR 0043 / `completion_verifier.md:68-94`, not evidence-recovery loss.\n\nDefect legitimacy: the historical untagged verdict is intended behavior. The generic remediation wording is a defect because it directs callers to a retry that cannot satisfy an untagged external criterion. Per rebar-debug, no Phase-2 edit to `completion_recovery.py` or `completion_verifier_finalizer.md` is authorized by the evidence. Next: replicate `verify-completion 8322` with the exact tag, then either close/reclassify this ticket if the blocker is gone or re-scope it to the remediation wording under a fresh plan review.","timestamp":1786067545030457001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report\n\nProblem: 8322 completion verification rejected concrete Gerrit/CI ticket evidence after a genuine-breadth primary exhaustion.\n\nProven cause/classification: the recorded retry was untagged. Its FAIL event timestamp was 1786063291486790001; the exact `[operator-attested]` edit followed at 1786063328784010001. ADR 0043 and `completion_verifier.md:81-86` require the exact tag and deliberately treat untagged criteria as codebase-verifiable. The recorded rejection was therefore intended behavior, not a recovery defect.\n\nProof: on current material, the unmodified production Sonnet recovery pipeline (current gatherer -> current finalizer, temperature 0) returned `kind=operator-attested, met=true` 3/3. A co-located-rule perturbation also passed 3/3, so it did not discriminate as a necessary recovery fix. Direct current-finalizer concrete evidence passed 3/3. The full command `rebar verify-completion 8322-6f05-ea1b-4da1 --output json` then reproduced the original genuine-breadth primary shape (240 requests, 243 tools, 241 distinct, max repeat 1; 1,879.7s), entered bounded recovery, and returned typed `PASS`, `certifiable=true`, `signable=true` for all nine criteria at attested `origin/main` SHA `9bdb22f5887ef4c03fed11d1fcefe952e70b3bd7`.\n\nTest/fix: no RED oracle or production fix was written because Phase 1 disproved the reported recovery defect; rebar-debug forbids crossing into Phase 2 without a confirmed defect. The temporary probe lived outside the repo and no repository files were changed.\n\nScope/safety: no caller behavior changed, no dependencies were added, and no tests were weakened. `origin/main` was fast-forwarded before ticket closure and includes upstream verifier change `53b9c3e6dd` (f6fc memo/nudge) plus `9bdb22f588`.\n\nResidual defect: `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:48-65` gives generic FAIL remediation saying ticket-comment evidence will be considered on retry but omits the exact-tag prerequisite for external evidence. That wording caused the futile comment-only retry. This is separate from the disproven recovery defect and should be tracked as remediation-contract drift.\n\nReplication: original close-path verifier no longer fails after the exact tag; it returned a certifiable PASS at default request/token settings with no force or budget override.","timestamp":1786069829363032001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 evidence\n\nFrozen oracle: the existing emitted-verdict interface test was strengthened to require the canonical `codebase-verifiable` kind, the exact `[operator-attested]` tag, an external/repository distinction, and the statement that an untagged external criterion cannot be satisfied by a ticket comment alone. Negative controls remain: PASS emits no remediation; FAIL guidance never advertises force.\n\nRED: `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py::test_fail_verdict_carries_remediation_guidance -q` collected/executed and failed at `assert \"[operator-attested]\" in guidance` against the old constant.\n\nHeld-out fix: fixer saw only the RCA and contract card; tests were removed/off-limits. It changed only `COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE`. Review then corrected one vocabulary issue (`repository-verifiable` -> canonical `codebase-verifiable`) under the test-modification guard: fix removed, final oracle revised, RED re-proven, corrected fix reapplied.\n\nGREEN: `tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py` => 23 passed. Defect-seeded mutation restoring the old guidance verbatim returned the held-out node to RED at the missing-tag assertion; restoring the fix returned it to GREEN. The oracle asserts emitted `verdict.remediation`, so behavior-preserving private refactors do not affect it.\n\nSafety/review: caller sweep found only `reconcile_verdict` plus deterministic/interface tests. No verdict logic, schemas, prompts, dependencies, security boundary, or performance path changed. Five-axis review found and resolved the one canonical-vocabulary issue; no remaining findings. No sibling construct/parity surface exists because every FAIL path converges through `reconcile_verdict`.\n\nGates: focused interface file 23 passed; `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed (438 source files); `make test` passed with 10,815 passed, 38 skipped, 228 deselected, 36 warnings in 2,183.62s. Ticket 8322 closed successfully without force after the tagged default verifier returned a certifiable PASS.","timestamp":1786072788731163001}],"created_at":1785456638624649001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a852744e-b361-415f-90b9-12f0c4743bde","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"94b4-059e-a74a-4cf8"},{"link_uuid":"d0af1a2c-c403-4eca-9ec1-6ece0e941221","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d251-65ef-7729-4f49"},{"link_uuid":"7fe5286a-cca2-450c-8014-42e95e71488e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"70bc-ab05-6d4c-45a0"},{"link_uuid":"85502114-4ffd-4e91-9a2d-2a60eff4878e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"60c2-9b55-1313-4029"}],"description":"## Context / Proven Defect\n\nThe 8322 close incident was rebar-debugged to a strict-tag ordering issue, not a recovery failure. The second verifier FAIL occurred at event timestamp 1786063291486790001 while the Gerrit criterion was still untagged; the exact `[operator-attested]` edit followed 37.30 seconds later at 1786063328784010001. ADR 0043 and `completion_verifier.md:81-86` intentionally treat every untagged criterion as codebase-verifiable, so rejecting ticket-only external evidence was correct.\n\nThe actionable defect is `COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE` in `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:48-65`. It tells every FAIL caller that adding concrete evidence to a ticket comment will be considered on retry, but omits the exact `[operator-attested]` tag prerequisite for evidence that inherently lives outside the repository. The operator followed that incomplete guidance and incurred a second 240-request verifier run that could not pass by contract.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Preserve the generic guidance and existing no-force posture.\n- State the two evidence channels affirmatively: repository-verifiable criteria require repository evidence (a comment may point the verifier to it); external evidence is admissible from a concrete ticket attestation only when the criterion begins with the exact `[operator-attested]` tag.\n- Keep malformed or untagged criteria on the existing codebase-verifiable default; do not weaken ADR 0043 injection boundaries or completion judgment.\n- Strengthen the existing interface test for FAIL remediation so it requires the exact tag prerequisite and the untagged-external fallback.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED: the existing remediation interface test, strengthened to require `operator-attested`, the exact tag, and the untagged external-evidence limitation, fails against current guidance.\n- GREEN: focused interface test passes after the guidance-only change.\n- Run focused completion-verifier interface tests, lint, typecheck, and the default test suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every FAIL remediation distinguishes repository-verifiable evidence from external operator-attested evidence.\n- [ ] The remediation names the exact `[operator-attested]` tag prerequisite and says an untagged external criterion cannot be satisfied by a ticket comment alone.\n- [ ] The guidance remains generic, does not advertise force/bypass, and does not change completion-verdict semantics.\n- [ ] The strengthened remediation interface test is observed RED before the fix and GREEN after it.\n- [ ] Lint, typecheck, and the default test suite pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"clarify exact operator-attested tag prerequisite in generic FAIL remediation"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py","reason":"strengthen remediation contract test with exact-tag and untagged-external controls"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","60c2-9b55-1313-4029"],["relates_to","70bc-ab05-6d4c-45a0"],["relates_to","d251-65ef-7729-4f49"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f27591ee-0c18-4041-8b0e-bf91a8cba6fc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["release-blocker","llm","completion-gate"],"ticket_id":"a89d-4dd2-f421-417a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion FAIL remediation omits operator-attested tag prerequisite","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["88ae292e-5721-44d0-bf37-e43f96c004c4","a852744e-b361-415f-90b9-12f0c4743bde","36102de5-c23d-4820-9fb8-68781542e42f","d0af1a2c-c403-4eca-9ec1-6ece0e941221","7fe5286a-cca2-450c-8014-42e95e71488e","9c06a0aa-94da-4537-bcd5-e7f6c4241cc7","938148a7-0c21-4eb4-a8d4-0d1485ca3310","3eac4c7c-9a8a-487f-8b4d-7e6dc658c161","78be0879-ea9b-4c5e-a173-01da03485ead","c75d71f3-2f8d-4289-8a6c-b8b562991c63","4938522f-8e7a-4b0f-ac22-6175d1d22f75","083661aa-92fe-4096-bf69-defb3111af3b","4890eb89-918b-42e3-8599-2c59dce63827","7dd68a27-601e-4023-9b51-3ebe03a4984b","f27591ee-0c18-4041-8b0e-bf91a8cba6fc","be96ae77-138e-4e25-ac7c-ca87977bab0a","221acc70-5d2a-4e78-a3f5-96df7ee36475","0a2010ac-b2af-4422-b71a-878aa5d6566e","b62552a3-66a0-4c01-9e82-6ed96a6caaf0","32fa1fb0-8621-4511-9ac1-0d8883d33158","3f6e8960-629a-4007-ab66-8d90556cf347","9c3f667d-45a3-4695-aa25-f8870f60a622","85502114-4ffd-4e91-9a2d-2a60eff4878e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786073088097763552,"uuid":"ef62664a-dbbd-49f3-95c0-2f7503085001"}